@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# y0d report: the phone's choices screen
+
+## Summary
+
+Added `choicesProvider`, `ChoicesOverlay`/`ChoicesScreen`, the `PhoneText.choices*` strings, `Capability.choices` in the
+phone's hello, and dropped it again from `ownPlayerIdentity`. New test file `choices_screen_test.dart`: 28 tests (14 per
+look, menu and TV), all pass. `tools/mine.sh`: format, analyze and party_host pass; controller_app has ONE failure,
+below.
+
+**Blocked:** `controller_app/test/phone_metrics_test.dart:305-315` pins the hello's capability list
+(`metrics, rating, layout, status, view, identity, night`). `Capability.choices` after `view` (the brief's item 4)
+breaks it. The file is not in `allow:`, so I did not touch it. The fix is one line: add `Capability.choices,` after
+`Capability.view,` in that list (and "seven" in the test name becomes "eight"). Until then mine.sh fails on that one test.
+
+Files:
+- `providers/choices.dart` (new, exported from `providers.dart`): `ChoicesState` and `ChoicesNotifier`; methods `pick`,
+  `step`, `lock`, `undo` send a `ChoicePickMessage` with the full held state. Cleared on ViewStarted, on a dropped link,
+  and `choicesResultHoldMs` (3000 ms) after the end. A same-round message updates it (held state taken from the
+  message), another round replaces it; a message of an already ended round is ignored.
+- `ui/choices_screen.dart` (new): cards, countdown + "Paused" chip, lock button, result. Toy look tokens only.
+- `ui/controller_screen.dart`: import, `resultShown` also true while a round shows, `ChoicesOverlay` in the Stack
+  (5 changed lines; file ends at 372 lines).
+- `storage.dart`: `Capability.choices` in the hello list. `host/hosting.dart`: `ownPlayerIdentity` drops it too (dartdoc).
+- `phone_text.dart`: `choicesPaused/LockIn/Locked/Default/NoChoice/Seconds/CostEach/YouGot/ChosenForYou`.
+- `test/support/fakes.dart`: FakeClient `choicePicks`, `choicesRound(...)`, `choicesEnd(...)`, `sendChoicePick`.
+  The brief's name `choices(ChoicesMessage)` would clash with the client's `choices` stream getter, so the feed is
+  `choicesRound`.
+
+## Decisions
+- ControllerScreen shows "too small" under 540 dp width (`minWindowWidth`), so 360x640 and 320x640 are tested with
+  `ChoicesOverlay` alone as a widget; 667x375 is tested inside the app (and the pad-back and dropped-link tests too).
+- Countdown clock is `client.nowMs` (fake-able), ticked by a 1 s timer in the widget; paused shows `endsInMs` as is.
+- Minus at 1 and plus at maxCount are greyed and swallow the tap (a no-op `onTap`), so the tap does not fall through to
+  the card and clear it. Plus on an unpicked counted card picks it with 1.
+- Lock with nothing picked is allowed (sends pick null, locked true). Picks while the round is paused are allowed.
+- The result card sits in a scroll view: the pop-in's first frames overflowed 17 px in the TV look at 667x375.
+
+## Computed values (tests)
+Counts after four plus taps on maxCount 3: [1, 2, 3]; then three minus taps: [1, 2, 3, 2, 1]. Countdown: 12000 ms,
+nowMs 3000 -> "9 s"; paused 9000 ms, nowMs 8000 -> still "9 s". Result visible at 2900 ms, gone at 3100 ms.
+
+## Self-check (R part A)
+1. Host setups: phone joined to a TV (every test, via `pumpApp`); host phone's own player: `ownPlayerIdentity` drops
+   choices (joined_view_test pin unchanged and passes); "Show on this device" and an older peer: not tested here (the
+   host sends the round only to phones that list the capability).
+2. State starts at a ChoicesMessage, ends 3 s after the end, on ViewStarted or a dropped link: "the overlay is gone 3 s
+   after the end", "a dropped link clears the round". Nothing going on: overlay is `SizedBox.shrink`.
+3. Pause menu / host away / "Get ready": not covered; the round pauses via the message's `paused` flag ("countdown ...
+   Paused"). Dropped link and leaving: clears. Results: the end texts test.
+4. Stayed in allow:, except Blocked above.
+5. Stopped on phone_metrics_test.dart (not in allow).
+6. Every look: all tests run in the menu look and the TV look; no fixed pixel height on cards; the 48 dp rule is tested
+   at 360x640, 320x640, 667x375.
+
+## Questions
+1. Q1/Q3 defaults from the brief are host-side; nothing here depends on them.
+2. Should the round cover the top bar (it does now), or leave it visible?
+
+## Hand-over
+Update `phone_metrics_test.dart` as above, then mine.sh is green. No `tests-first` proof needed beyond the new file.
+
+## Commit message
+
+phone: generic choices screen (cards, countdown, lock-in, result)
+
+choicesProvider keeps the host's choice round and what this phone holds;
+ChoicesOverlay shows it over the pad (cards, counted cards, countdown,
+Paused, Lock in/Locked, result lines). The phone lists Capability.choices;
+the host phone's own player drops it and plays through the old buttons.
+
+## Status row
+
+phone1b y0d: phone choices screen, provider, strings and capability done; open: phone_metrics_test.dart hello pin needs `Capability.choices` (outside allow).
+
+## Delete
+
+- none
